// StreamMasterdataEventsParams defines parameters for StreamMasterdataEvents.
type StreamMasterdataEventsParams struct {
	// LastEventID The event id the application saved last from `/masterdata/events` stream, as agrirouter issued it in the `id:` field of an SSE frame. The application MUST send it back exactly as issued, treat it as an opaque string and MUST NOT interpret, compare, construct, or modify it in any way. Its structure is not defined by this API and may change; the example below illustrates its size and shape only.
	// It does not always advance on every frame: the same value may repeat on some frames, and an application MUST NOT read anything into that beyond its own position for `Last-Event-ID` being unchanged.
	//
	// The application MUST save it from what it has **durably applied** rather than from whatever its stream client last read; delivery is at-least-once, so everything after it is sent again on reconnect. Where applies complete out of order, store the id of the earliest frame, in the order the stream delivered them, that is not yet applied: ids are not comparable by the application, so this is a matter of remembering delivery order. It does not expire, and agrirouter stores no copy of it.
	//
	// Omitted, or present and one agrirouter cannot validate, is served as a first connection on this stream: everything the application is entitled to, ending with a `CAUGHT_UP` frame. That costs the application its place in the stream and not its entitlement, and is how it asks for every entity to be delivered again.
	//
	// This parameter applies to `/masterdata/events` only. The initial-load stream carries no position and does not accept it.
	LastEventID *LastEventId `json:"Last-Event-ID,omitempty"`
}

